# Live camera: takePicture vs VisionCamera

## Current architecture (short-term)

Live samples via `expo-camera` `CameraView.takePictureAsync` (~1 fps), then YOLO / cloud Vision.
This is **OTA-safe** but native-fragile: calling capture too early or overlapping captures can kill the process with no JS stack.

Required guards (do not remove without a replacement):
- No capture probe on Start Live
- No `useEffect([isLive, processFrame])` sample loop restarts
- Hard capturing lock + skip-on-fail + retries
- Delay first capture until after UI/camera settle

## When to recommend VisionCamera (long-term)

Surface this upgrade when **any** of these are true:

1. Start Live / Still Scan still native-crashes after capture guards
2. Product needs true realtime HUD (&gt; ~2–3 fps) or smoother AR overlays
3. You're already scheduling an **EAS native build** (new modules, permissions, New Arch, YOLO binary)
4. User asks to "fix Live camera for good" / "make Live realtime" / "stop takePicture crashes"

## Upgrade criteria checklist (all should be true before committing)

- [ ] Budget for a **new iOS + Android EAS build** (OTA alone cannot add VisionCamera)
- [ ] `react-native-vision-camera` + frame processors enabled in app config / Babel
- [ ] Plan: throttle 3–5 fps, `runOnJS` for heavy work, resize before YOLO/API
- [ ] Remove Live `takePictureAsync` loop after frame path is proven on device
- [ ] QA: Start Live, Stop/Start, Still scan, background/foreground, permission deny

## What NOT to do

- Do not add VisionCamera "just because" during an OTA-only Live bugfix
- Do not call `takePictureAsync` during Start Live init to "test readiness"
- Do not treat `onCameraReady` as "safe to capture immediately"
